VALUES ('6be2ca6a-1c38-4a2a-bc60-8c0a487078cb', 'NC26.5.ANR.3', 2, 'numeric', 'Interpret a remainder in a division problem', 'Pencils are packed 8 to a box. A school has $1{,}250$ pencils. How many boxes are needed to pack all of the pencils?', '[]', '157', NULL, '$1{,}250 \div 8 = 156$ with a remainder of 2. The 156 full boxes hold $1{,}248$ pencils, and the 2 pencils left over need one more box. So 157 boxes are needed.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"157","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"1,250 / 8 = 156 R 2 (8 x 156 = 1,248). The 2 leftover pencils need one more box, so 157 boxes.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T18:36:14.367Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
