VALUES ('9d49dab1-86e0-4dd7-9029-194641b547f9', 'NC26.5.SGMR.4', 3, 'numeric', 'How volume changes when the edges are doubled', 'A cube has a volume of 27 cubic centimeters. A second cube has edges that are twice as long as the edges of the first cube. What is the volume of the second cube, in cubic centimeters?', '[]', '216', '(2*3)^3', 'The first cube has edges of 3 cm because $3 \times 3 \times 3 = 27$. The second cube has edges of 6 cm, so its volume is $6 \times 6 \times 6 = 216$ cubic centimeters.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"216","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"First cube edge 3 cm (3 x 3 x 3 = 27). Second edge 6 cm: 6 x 6 x 6 = 216.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T18:36:14.367Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
